<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat-Rains slow Montana harvest.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat-Rains slow Montana harvest.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rains slowed hard red winter wheat harvest in parts of Montana on Monday but drier weather was expected to speed progress later this week, several cash grain dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;We're just waiting for the rain to clear up so we can get back into harvest,&quot; a Montana dealer said. &quot;We should be clear in the next couple of days.&quot;</p>
<p>Bids for dark northern spring and hard red winter wheat were mostly lower in reaction to losses in MGE and KCBT futures, the dealers said.</p>
<p>Spring wheat conditions were of growing concern.</p>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department on Monday said 43 percent of the spring wheat crop was in good to excellent condition, down from 50 percent the previous week.</p>
